{"id": "evt_ce0b132f3ae5", "entity_type": "question", "entity_id": "qst_49961d378034", "action": "updated", "actor_id": "TNqEfA0eOGOLB2Peufu8yA1ZFhB3", "payload": {"type": "forum", "responses": [], "id": "qst_49961d378034", "symptoms_summary": "", "title": "My stroke medications", "created_at": "2026-05-01T06:15:41.222218Z", "bookmark_count": 0, "ai_summary": "Open forum request tagged Neurology, English, Related to my medications.", "premium": false, "author_id": "YjAuMPiqUBfy0oJiVNfK445JdhN2", "attachment_ids": ["att_1c36ff7417f4"], "updated_at": "2026-05-01T06:16:49.318037+00:00", "current_diagnosis_text": null, "upvote_count": 0, "heading_group": "Related to my medications", "tags": ["Neurology", "English", "Related to my medications", "Forum"], "is_public": true, "payment_status": "not_required", "status": "open", "target_doctor_id": "TNqEfA0eOGOLB2Peufu8yA1ZFhB3", "language": "English", "body": "Doctor, I had stroke in 2025. I was treated by you at Aster Hospital. I was admitted for 3 days. After that I have been taking medicines, such as aspirin, bp medicines, cholesterol medicines. I wanted to know how long to continue these medications? I have been told that once you start BP medicines, you have to continue it lifelong, but now my BP is normal; should I continue the bp medicine?"}, "created_at": "2026-05-01T06:16:49.931844Z"}
{"id": "evt_bebc73199e8b", "entity_type": "response", "entity_id": "rsp_46b04d25fe9a", "action": "created", "actor_id": "TNqEfA0eOGOLB2Peufu8yA1ZFhB3", "payload": {"id": "rsp_46b04d25fe9a", "question_id": "qst_49961d378034", "doctor_id": "TNqEfA0eOGOLB2Peufu8yA1ZFhB3", "labels": ["Educational", "General guidance", "Opinion only"], "key_points": "Medicines should be continued, some of them lifelong;\nBP is normal because of medications", "what_it_means": "Take decisions in consultation with your doctor", "what_to_discuss_with_doctor": "BP control\nRationalizing the medicines for stroke prevention.", "full_text": "Hi, Raj! Thanks for asking this question. I do remember seeing you in the hospital. Very happy to note that you are currently back to normal life. Regarding your questions about medications, the simple answer is that preventive treatment for stroke should be continued lifelong; this may means some medicines. Over time, the need for some medicines may decrease, or they may be stopped entirely, but some medicines may have to be continued lifelong. We can discuss this in more details and specifically in person, or with any neurologist that you can meet at your convenience. Regarding the BP medicines, my suggestion is to continue it for now till you meet a doctor. Control of BP is in a important cornerstone for prevention of stroke; though BP control can be achieved with lifestyle and diet change, you do need to be careful and keep a closer watch on the BP on a more regular basis. Occasionally medicines for BP can be stopped successfully because your diet and exercise is sufficient to control it - but this would require a more frequent check of BP and should be done only under supervision. Hope this answers your question. Please do not hesitate to ask follow up questions or raise other questions as and when you have any doubts.", "response_mode": "text", "created_at": "2026-05-01T07:53:35.917985Z"}, "created_at": "2026-05-01T07:53:41.241703Z"}
